<article class="env-lemma" id="085R">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/085R">Lemma <span data-tag="085R">71.17.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $\mathcal{I} \subset \mathcal{O}_ X$ be a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals. Let $U = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ be an affine scheme étale over $X$ and let $I \subset A$ be the ideal corresponding to $\mathcal{I}|_ U$. If $X' \to X$ is the blowup of $X$ in $\mathcal{I}$, then there is a canonical isomorphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  U \times _ X X' = \text{Proj}(\bigoplus \nolimits _{d \geq 0} I^ d)  \]
</div>
  <p> of schemes over $U$, where the right hand side is the homogeneous spectrum of the Rees algebra of $I$ in $A$. Moreover, $U \times _ X X'$ has an affine open covering by spectra of the affine blowup algebras $A[\frac{I}{a}]$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Note that the restriction $\mathcal{I}|_ U$ is equal to the pullback of $\mathcal{I}$ via the morphism $U \to X$, see Properties of Spaces, Section <a href="/tag/03LT" data-tag="03LT">66.26</a>. Thus the lemma follows on combining Lemma <a href="/tag/084B" data-tag="084B">71.11.2</a> with Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/0804" data-tag="0804">31.33.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>